      the real-to-complex Fourier transform satisfies the conjugate symmetry,
      i.e., :math:`X[m, \omega] = X[m, \text{n\_fft} - \omega]^*`.
      Note if the input or window tensors are complex, then :attr:`onesided`
      output is not possible.

